---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Epistemic Audit"
  description="We show what was left out. An epistemic audit checks what a document claims to know, and what it leaves out."
>
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>We show what was left out.</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">An epistemic audit checks what a document claims to know, and what it leaves out. One written finding per point, with the source in your own text.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <p><strong>We bring the audit to you, in your building, offline. Your documents stay with you.</strong></p>
      <p><strong>For small firms, law and accountancy practices, charities, schools, councils and other public bodies.</strong></p>
      <p><strong>Based in Lampeter, Wales. We visit within 60 road miles, and up to 120 miles by arrangement.</strong></p>
      <p><em>Conversations can be booked now; visits from February 2027.</em></p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 48px;">How a visit works</h2>
      <ol class="steps-list">
        <li><strong>Start.</strong> We switch on one machine in front of you. It shows its fingerprint on screen, and the same fingerprint is printed on your signed visit record.</li>
        <li><strong>Offline.</strong> The machine is fully offline, sealed from the internet and from your network. We show you.</li>
        <li><strong>Your documents in.</strong> On your own USB stick.</li>
        <li><strong>Your finding, before we leave.</strong> The written finding of what was left out, with sources, on paper or a fresh stick.</li>
        <li><strong>Wiped clean.</strong> The machine is wiped clean in front of you.</li>
        <li><strong>Signed visit record.</strong> What came in, what went out, who was present, when it was wiped clean. We both sign; you keep a signed visit record of what was checked.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 48px;">What you get</h2>
      <p>One written finding per document. For each point: what was left out, why it matters, and the source in your own text.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 48px;">One finding, shown — from a two-page public notice by a law firm on its use of an AI tool</h2>
      
      <div class="finding-example">
        <h3>What was left out</h3>
        <p>How long the documents a client uploads to the tool are kept, and when they are deleted. The notice says personal data may be in them, then stops.</p>

        <h3>Why it matters</h3>
        <p>Retention is the first question a careful client asks; the second is who else has a copy. The notice does not answer the first, and its privacy-notice link does not say where to look.</p>

        <h3>Source</h3>
        <p>The notice's own paragraph on uploaded documents as published; its privacy-notice link names no section. One of 14 findings; the fix is one sentence.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="caption">Sample audit of a public document, October 2026, redacted.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 48px;">What it costs</h2>
      <p>Published prices.</p>

      <div class="pricing-table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Visit</th>
              <th>Price</th>
              <th>What it covers</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Audit Visit — half a day, up to 3 documents</td>
              <td>£750 + VAT</td>
              <td>Up to three documents of up to 20 pages each</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Audit Day — up to 10 documents</td>
              <td>£2,500 + VAT</td>
              <td>Up to ten documents, plus a page on the gaps they share</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Monthly visit</td>
              <td>from £1,000 a month + VAT</td>
              <td>Up to four documents; we show what changed since last month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Free first conversation — 45 minutes, by phone or in person</td>
              <td>Free</td>
              <td>You tell us what you need; we can show the method on a public document you choose</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p class="pricing-note">On-site within 60 road miles of Lampeter; travel included. Up to 120 miles, £150 + VAT a visit.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 48px;">What you provide</h2>
      <ul class="terms-list">
        <li>A private room, a power socket and your own USB stick.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 48px;">Terms of a visit</h2>
      <ul class="terms-list">
        <li><strong>Notice:</strong> 10 working days for a first visit, so your IT or security team can sign off; we send a one-page device statement. Monthly visits are booked three months ahead on a fixed day.</li>
        <li><strong>You provide:</strong> a private room with a table, one UK power socket, and your documents on your own USB stick.</li>
        <li><strong>Audit Visit:</strong> at most 4 hours on site; one written finding per document of up to 20 pages each (up to 3 documents).</li>
        <li><strong>Audit Day:</strong> at most 7 hours on site; one written finding per document (up to 10 documents), plus a page on the gaps they share.</li>
        <li><strong>Monthly visit:</strong> at most 4 hours on site; up to four documents; we show what changed since last month's audit.</li>
        <li><strong>Cancellation:</strong> free to move or cancel up to 5 working days before. Later than that, or if there is no room or no one from your team on the day, the fee carries to one new date within 60 days. If we cancel, you choose a full refund or a new date.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment:</strong> private firms pay on booking; public bodies by purchase order, invoiced on the day at 30 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Travel:</strong> on-site within 60 road miles of Lampeter; travel included. Up to 120 miles, £150 + VAT a visit.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="cta-banner" style="margin-top: 48px;">
        <h3 style="margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Book a conversation</h3>
        <p style="margin: 0 0 20px 0;">It starts with a free 45-minute conversation. You tell us what you need; we can show the method on a public document you choose.</p>
        <a href="mailto:info@cogniosynthesisportal.uk?subject=Epistemic%20Audit%20conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Email to book</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f6f3f0 0%, #ebe7e4 100%);
    padding: 80px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e0dcd8;
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: 48px;
    color: #0e1020;
    margin: 0 0 16px 0;
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: #4b4d5d;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .steps-list, .terms-list {
    padding-left: 24px;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }

  .steps-list li, .terms-list li {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #4b4d5d;
    line-height: 28px;
  }

  .finding-example {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #dcdce0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 32px;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }

  .finding-example h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #0e1020;
    margin: 24px 0 12px 0;
  }

  .finding-example h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .finding-example p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #4b4d5d;
    line-height: 28px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .caption {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #4b4d5d;
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }

  .pricing-table table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .pricing-table th,
  .pricing-table td {
    padding: 16px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dcdce0;
  }

  .pricing-table th {
    background: #f6f3f0;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #0e1020;
  }

  .pricing-note {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #4b4d5d;
  }

  .cta-banner {
    background: #f6f3f0;
    padding: 32px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .cta-banner h3 {
    font-size: 24px;
    color: #0e1020;
    margin: 0 0 16px 0;
  }

  .cta-banner p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #4b4d5d;
    line-height: 28px;
  }
</style>
